+{"scenarios":[{"id":"invoice","title":"Invoice payment","kicker":"Pay part. Keep the remainder visible.","summary":"Follow one payment through seller receipt, the source fee, and the duties left in escrow.","utility":"Explain exactly what the buyer funds, what the seller receives, and what is still owed.","status":"PROPOSED","strands":[{"id":"invoice-payment","label":"Payment arithmetic","claim":"The seller payment matches the chosen partial amount.","statement":"Opening invoice duty 100 CASH; payment 35 CASH; escrow debit for payment and fee 37 CASH.","authentication":"The worksheet supplies an illustrative opening state; an application would need its actual predecessor and exact CASH identity.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"invoice-fee","label":"Fee accounting","claim":"The 2 CASH source fee is a separate payment.","statement":"Escrow pays seller 35 CASH and fees 2 CASH; the fee does not discharge invoice duty.","authentication":"Source S12 names escrow, seller, fees, and CASH; actual outputs still need the consuming validator.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"invoice-duty","label":"Duty continuation","claim":"Partial payment preserves the unpaid invoice and reserve duty.","statement":"Invoice 100 − 35 = 65 CASH; reserve duty remains 10 CASH; total duties 75 CASH.","authentication":"The starting duty amounts are worksheet premises; a real application must bind them to its predecessor.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"}],"effects":["Source-funded cash 110 − payment 35 − fee 2 = 73 CASH; duties total 75 CASH, a backing gap of 2 CASH.","Proposed extra funding gives cash 112 − 35 − 2 = 75 CASH, matching duties for this one partial.","The source partial action requires 0 < amount < opening invoice duty. Paying the whole invoice uses finish(), which has different fee behavior."],"dependencies":["These are future proof roles, not three existing proof producers.","Funding 112 is a proposed backing policy; S12 contains no extra-funding action.","Every further partial charges another 2 CASH. One extra fee budget does not fund a sequence of partials.","The source has no reserve-duty-return action. Staged delivery and recovery need additional implementation."],"sourceRefs":[{"label":"Invoice source: open / partial / finish","document":"S12-installment-invoice.mori","pointer":"actions open, partial, finish"},{"label":"Selected invoice walkthrough","document":"CONCEPT.md","pointer":"#a-first-reference-app-that-teaches-the-model"},{"label":"Invoice page copy","document":"MESSAGING.md","pointer":"#show-the-payment-show-the-fee-show-what-remains"},{"label":"CL-20","document":"CLAIMS-REGISTER.json","pointer":"/claims/19"},{"label":"CL-26","document":"CLAIMS-REGISTER.json","pointer":"/claims/25"},{"label":"Opus 5.5 ERR-22","document":"SECURITY-ERRATA.json","pointer":"/rows/21"},{"label":"Opus 5.5 ERR-28","document":"SECURITY-ERRATA.json","pointer":"/rows/27"}]},{"id":"dex","title":"Exchange orders","kicker":"Give every order its own outcome.","summary":"Connect each order’s exact assets and minimum net receipt to a specified pool transition.","utility":"Let a batch builder explain each owner’s result alongside the shared pool arithmetic.","status":"PROPOSED","strands":[{"id":"dex-orders","label":"Order arithmetic","claim":"Each illustrated order meets its own amount bounds.","statement":"Two orders each offer 100 A and require at least 90 B net; the illustration assigns each owner 92 B.","authentication":"Exact asset identities, owner limits, and actual outputs must be supplied and bound by a real application.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"dex-pool","label":"Pool arithmetic","claim":"A supported pool relation explains the pool continuation.","statement":"The chosen reserve update, fee rule, and exact rounding must agree with the two illustrated orders.","authentication":"No pool reserve or price observation is supplied here; pool state provenance remains a required input.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate. No pool computation or verified price is shown.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"dex-batch","label":"Batch accounting","claim":"Order and pool amounts agree across the batch.","statement":"The same amounts used for each owner’s result must appear in the batch accounting.","authentication":"Actual output allocation belongs to the consuming validator under its selected profile.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate. The strict illustration uses a separate output per order; coalesced-payment partition is a separate policy choice.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"}],"effects":["Each illustrated owner gives 100 A and receives 92 B net against a minimum of 90 B.","Pool balances, fees, and rounding need a complete independent worksheet before execution.","A partial fill must retain unfilled quantity and duties; cancellation is a separate action."],"dependencies":["Identify supported order and pool relations and their actual proof producers.","Choose and enforce actual-output allocation for the consumer’s profile.","Supply exact asset, recipient, fee, rounding, continuation, and cancellation rules."],"sourceRefs":[{"label":"Two-order allocation target","document":"S02-PATTERN-INVENTORY.json","pointer":"/11"},{"label":"Pool rounding target","document":"S02-PATTERN-INVENTORY.json","pointer":"/9"},{"label":"Order cancellation target","document":"S02-PATTERN-INVENTORY.json","pointer":"/10"},{"label":"Selected DEX case","document":"CONCEPT.md","pointer":"#five-application-cases"},{"label":"CL-22","document":"CLAIMS-REGISTER.json","pointer":"/claims/21"},{"label":"CL-51","document":"CLAIMS-REGISTER.json","pointer":"/claims/50"},{"label":"Opus 5.5 ERR-08","document":"SECURITY-ERRATA.json","pointer":"/rows/7"},{"label":"Opus 5.5 ERR-23","document":"SECURITY-ERRATA.json","pointer":"/rows/22"}]},{"id":"issuance","title":"Token issuance","kicker":"Show where every issued unit goes.","summary":"Keep application-asset supply, recipient distribution, and any servicing promises distinct.","utility":"Give an issuer an inspectable account of new supply and the obligations attached to it.","status":"PROPOSED","strands":[{"id":"issuance-supply","label":"Supply arithmetic","claim":"The proposed supply update stays within the cap.","statement":"Illustrative first issue: 300 application-asset units under a cap of 1,000; unissued capacity is 700.","authentication":"The issuer policy, exact application asset, and supply predecessor need an actual authenticated path.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"issuance-distribution","label":"Distribution arithmetic","claim":"The recipient allocation totals the issued amount.","statement":"Recipient one receives 180 units and recipient two receives 120 units; 180 + 120 = 300.","authentication":"Recipient identities and actual mint and payment outputs must be enforced by the applicable policies and validators.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"issuance-duties","label":"Duty accounting","claim":"Servicing duties remain separate from token supply.","statement":"The remaining 700 units of issue capacity are not debt. A redemption promise is a duty only when explicitly defined.","authentication":"Any servicing promise needs named parties, an exact asset, and a defined creation and discharge rule.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate. This illustration supplies no redemption agreement.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"}],"effects":["Application-asset issuance is 300 units: 180 to one recipient and 120 to the other.","Unissued capacity is 700 units, with no debt inferred from that capacity.","Issuing a proof claim token does not mint the application asset."],"dependencies":["Implement supported application mint/burn semantics and actual mint-policy enforcement.","Continue supply state and bind exact recipients and assets.","Define any separate redemption duty; external eligibility documents retain their issuer and freshness assumptions."],"sourceRefs":[{"label":"Supply and liability meanings","document":"S03-MORIARTY-PRODUCT-CONTRACT.md","pointer":"#what-provable-intention-means"},{"label":"Selected issuance case","document":"CONCEPT.md","pointer":"#five-application-cases"},{"label":"Issuance page card","document":"MESSAGING.md","pointer":"#five-use-case-cards"},{"label":"CL-23","document":"CLAIMS-REGISTER.json","pointer":"/claims/22"}]},{"id":"loan","title":"Loan repayment","kicker":"Separate repayment from its fee.","summary":"Show principal, accrual, payment, fee, and remaining debt as different amounts.","utility":"Help borrower and lender inspect how a payment changes the outstanding duty.","status":"PROPOSED","strands":[{"id":"loan-accrual","label":"Accrual arithmetic","claim":"The defined period’s accrual updates opening debt.","statement":"Illustrative debt 100 CASH plus accrual 5 CASH gives a duty of 105 CASH.","authentication":"The agreement must supply the period, rate, rounding, and provenance of any variable-rate observation.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate. No rate source or live accrual is supplied.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"loan-payment","label":"Payment accounting","claim":"Payment and fee retain their different meanings.","statement":"Debt payment 35 CASH plus separate fee 2 CASH gives payer gross debit 37 CASH.","authentication":"The actual payer, lender, fee recipient, and exact asset must agree with owner authorization and transaction effects.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"},{"id":"loan-duty","label":"Debt continuation","claim":"Only the payment discharges the debt.","statement":"Duty 105 − repayment 35 = 70 CASH remaining; the fee 2 is not repayment.","authentication":"A real continuation must bind the predecessor duty and its explicit accrual and discharge entries.","limits":"Illustrative requirement only: no concrete proof instance or independent producer is supplied. These arithmetic checks may share one whole-execution proof. Actual signatures and validator enforcement remain separate.","status":"ILLUSTRATIVE_FUTURE_PROOF_ROLE"}],"effects":["Opening debt 100 + accrual 5 = 105 CASH.","Payer gross debit is 37 CASH: repayment 35 and fee 2.","Closing debt is 70 CASH. Collateral release requires its own policy."],"dependencies":["Define period, rate, rounding, and any observation freshness rule.","Bind actual loan payments and the continuing debt to the authorized transition.","Supply separate origination and collateral policies; this lesson establishes no ACTUS conformance."],"sourceRefs":[{"label":"Origination target","document":"S02-PATTERN-INVENTORY.json","pointer":"/12"},{"label":"Interest-period target","document":"S02-PATTERN-INVENTORY.json","pointer":"/13"},{"label":"Partial repayment target","document":"S02-PATTERN-INVENTORY.json","pointer":"/14"},{"label":"Gross/fee/net target","document":"S02-PATTERN-INVENTORY.json","pointer":"/15"},{"label":"Typed duty accounting","document":"S03-MORIARTY-PRODUCT-CONTRACT.md","pointer":"#what-provable-intention-means"},{"label":"Selected loan case","document":"CONCEPT.md","pointer":"#five-application-cases"},{"label":"CL-24","document":"CLAIMS-REGISTER.json","pointer":"/claims/23"}]},{"id":"treasury","title":"Treasury allocation","kicker":"Follow the amounts into the reserve.","summary":"Separate allocation arithmetic, actual transfers, and the duties that remain afterward.","utility":"Make the beneficiary amounts, fee budget, and reserve or rebate duties visible to owners.","status":"PROPOSED","strands":[{"id":"treasury-quotient","label":"Quotient arithmetic","claim":"The allocation inputs