are resolved by the consumer from its pinned profile; bundle-supplied roots are refused.\",\n    \"universal-property entries are certificates bound to program identity (layer 2), property hash, semantics, bounds and checker id; by reference only.\",\n    \"Aggregation or recursion is a separate relation with its own covered list; it changes no entry's kind, anchor or freshness.\",\n    \"Unsupported, unknown, timeout, missing entry, superseded version and digest mismatch fail closed.\",\n    \"The accepted predicate/relation/VK set is committed by contract state; migration only by a program-defined authorized action; a registry UTxO is an optional data store only.\",\n    \"Permissionless production; acceptance follows the consumer's own policy only: pinned catalogue manifest digest, pinned record log digest, accepted {predicate_ref -> vk_digest} map, vk deny-list, consumer-declared audit and dispute grants and required audit scopes (review A2, A4; fdecbe41 B1).\",\n    \"v1 bundles are AND of k in {1,2} entries; OR, k-of-n and DAG parents are specified elsewhere and not admitted here.\",\n    \"Every circuit-constant statement value equals the admission record's circuit_constants and any catalogue-pinned value; non-production keys are refused (review A3).\",\n    \"A bundle that names a program digest must contain an entry whose statement binds that digest (G16 audit F1).\",\n    \"vector-evidenced requires relation-observation and statement-binding within the record's effective scopes (record refs intersected with consumer grants for that key and predicate), an admitted record and no consumer or cited dispute (review fdecbe41 B1).\"\n  ],\n  \"settlementClassMapping\": [\n    {\n      \"claimKind\": \"ledger-current-context\",\n      \"class\": \"ledger claim\",\n      \"treatment\": \"recomputed by S_settle0 from TxInfo; no SNARK; never carried by a bundle\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claimKind\": \"computation\",\n      \"class\": \"run certificate\",\n      \"tre