e the catalogue's normative slot type; the circuit's snapshot representation is not established (circuit-friendly encoding missing).\"\n      },\n      \"anchorType\": \"none\",\n      \"semanticsId\": \"moriarty-core/1 hand-lowered action pay of payment.mori over P-L0\",\n      \"resultSchema\": \"accept/reject of the relation over the typed statement; no ledger result\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-VER-01\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"VER\",\n      \"title\": \"Groth16 over BLS12-381 verifiable in Plutus V3\",\n      \"property\": \"CIP-0381 builtins (G1/G2 add, scalarMul, neg, compress/uncompress, hashToGroup, millerLoop, mulMlResult, finalVerify) suffice to evaluate the Groth16 verification equation on chain.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"verifier-property\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"eras with these builtins\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"S-CIP381\",\n        \"S-G16\",\n        \"P-EP319\",\n        \"B-COST\",\n        \"X-G16REPORT\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"Statement scalars.\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"blst-backed builtin correctness; MlResult only from millerLoop, so e(alpha, beta) is not precomputable (4 Miller loops per T05).\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Per protocol version and cost model.\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Verifier with VK pinned in script.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"Spec observed; Preprod protocol 11.0 observed (MCP-OBS-02); external measurements recorded (MCP-REC-02). G16 experiment: Aiken/UPLC verification with CIP-0381 builtins only, 4 Miller loops, about 2.13e9 CPU / 13.6e3 mem under Aiken's built-in cost model, not the Preprod epoch-319 model [X-G16REPORT as quoted by S-REVIEW-CAT sec. 5; author-reported; independent full audit running; nothing here approves any cryptography].\",\n      \"status\": \"source-backed-candidate\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Measured fit of verifier plus digest plus context checks under the Preprod cost model.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Landing verifier for any Groth16 Moriarty claim on Cardano.\",\n      \"experiment\": \"T05 E3 work curve for n in {1,2,4,8,16,32} public inputs, loop versus MSM.\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"That a Midnight-native proof is Groth16-verifiable (it is PLONK/KZG).\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-VER-01@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-VER-01@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"G16-COND: Aiken-model cost, unaudited\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-VER-02\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"VER\",\n      \"title\": \"MSM builtin availability on Preprod\",\n      \"property\": \"bls12_381_G1_multiScalarMul is usable by Plutus V3 scripts on Preprod.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"verifier-property\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"Preprod epoch 319\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"S-CIP133\",\n        \"S-VANROSSEM\",\n        \"P-EP319\",\n        \"T10\",\n        \"S-REVIEW-CAT\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"n/a\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"Van Rossem activation at protocol 11 (glossary, T05); Preprod reports 11.0.\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Per protocol version.\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Replace per-input scalarMul loop; MSM fails on empty or unequal lists (T05).\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"Status lag, not contradiction: CIP-0133 page status Proposed [S-CIP133] vs the mainnet van Rossem glossary listing CIP-133 among PV11 builtins [S-VANROSSEM source-06.md:34-36]. Preprod PV 11.0 is provider-reported [P-EP319]. That builtins are gated by protocol version on Preprod exactly as on mainnet is [EXT].\",\n      \"status\": \"conditional-construction\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Cost-model entry names not mapped (MCP-OBS-02).\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Determines public-input budget.\",\n      \"experiment\": \"T05 E1 builtin pin, then a local evaluation using the Preprod cost model.\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"Availability on any other network.\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-VER-02@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-VER-02@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F13: status lag, not contradiction\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-VER-03\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"VER\",\n      \"title\": \"Public-input canonicality and exact count\",\n      \"property\": \"Verifier rejects any public scalar outside [0, r) and any count different from |IC| - 1.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"verifier-property\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"every verification\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"S-AK381\",\n        \"T05\",\n        \"T09\",\n        \"X-G16REPORT\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"Statement scalars.\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"Scalars are reduced mod group order before scalar multiplication (CIP-0133 per T05).\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"n/a\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Validator derives scalars itself and range-checks them.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"T05 code reading: ak-381 ignores trailing inputs and does not range-check (not executed). G16 X5: the raw check accepted x1+r in place of x1 [X-G16REPORT as quoted by S-REVIEW-CAT sec. 5; author-reported; independent full audit running; nothing here approves any cryptography]; research evidence that scalars must be validator-derived (MCP-REF-02@1).\",\n      \"status\": \"source-backed-candidate\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Hardened verifier and tests.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Aliasing x and x+r would let an amount alias another value.\",\n      \"experiment\": \"T05 E2 negative suite (x+r, extra input, missing input, bad flags, re-randomized proof, VK swap).\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"n/a\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-VER-03@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-VER-03@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"G16-COND: X5 scalar alias, unaudited\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-VER-04\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"VER\",\n      \"title\": \"Verifying-key and relation identity binding\",\n      \"property\": \"The verifier uses a VK fixed by the script (constant or parameter), or a redeemer-supplied VK whose vk_digest = BLAKE2b-256(canonical VK bytes) is checked against a consumer-pinned digest (review B R7). VK identity, setup class and transcripts live in an AdmissionRecord (moriarty-cardano-admission-record/1), never in the SemanticEntry; each vk_digest maps to exactly one (predicate_id, version).\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"verifier-property\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"contract lifetime\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"T05\",\n        \"T07\",\n        \"B-SCHEMA\",\n        \"S-REVIEW-CAT\",\n        \"S-REVIEW-B\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"vk_digest and setup class only as validator-supplied statement data, never as circuit constants.\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"At least one honest contributor in each phase; a Groth16 VK is not recomputable from the circuit alone.\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Upgrade only through a program-defined, authorized migration action [T07 s7].\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Setup model is a per-VK admission choice: (a) per-program phase-2 MPC open to contribution, including by relying counterparties, with a public transcript; (b) one bounded universal interpreter per semantics version under an open MPC (amortizes setup, concentrates forgery risk in one trapdoor); (c) universal-SRS or wrapper systems; (d) no setup (direct validator). Interpreter vs per-program is decided by measured census (synthesis rank 5) and the two-vote rule. Author-sole and class-0 VKs are refused for counterparty-protective policies (MCP-REF-08@1).\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"Midnight path re-derives VKs from source plus pinned SRS (per T07); no Groth16 equivalent.\",\n      \"status\": \"source-backed-candidate\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Per-VK setup decision (two agreeing substantive votes) and ceremony tooling.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Relation identity for proof bundles; prevents caller-chosen keys.\",\n      \"experiment\": \"T07 E1 two phase-2 runs give different VKs; T07 E4 upgrade and old-proof acceptance.\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"Honesty of any ceremony.\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-VER-04@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-VER-04@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F2: VK identity in AdmissionRecord only\",\n        \"F5: setup model is a per-VK admission choice\",\n        \"review-B R7/PVC-18\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-VER-05\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"VER\",\n      \"title\": \"Proof point validity\",\n      \"property\": \"Proof elements decode only to prime-order-subgroup points (CIP-0381 uncompress).\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"verifier-property\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"every verification\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"S-CIP381\",\n        \"T05\",\n        \"X-G16REPORT\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"n/a\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"Builtin correctness.\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"n/a\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Rely on builtin; decide an explicit point-at-infinity policy.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"Spec only. The G16 experiment reports that a bit-flipped point caused a builtin failure [X-G16REPORT as quoted by S-REVIEW-CAT sec. 5; author-reported; independent full audit running; nothing here approves any cryptography]. Infinity policy still undecided.\",\n      \"status\": \"source-backed-candidate\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Infinity policy undecided.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"n/a\",\n      \"experiment\": \"Non-subgroup and infinity encodings presented to the verifier.\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"n/a\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-VER-05@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-VER-05@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"G16-COND: bit-flipped point observation, unaudited\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-AST-02\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"AST\",\n      \"title\": \"Minting-policy acceptance versus asset meaning\",\n      \"property\": \"A mint of (p, n, q) in this transaction shows only that policy p accepted this transaction.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"ledger-current-context\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"current transaction\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"S-PV3CTX\",\n        \"B-REQ\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"n/a\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"Plutus V3 phase-2: the ledger constructs ScriptContext/TxInfo; no prover-supplied root. Relative to the chain fork the transaction is applied on; no finality. Field list per an unpinned plutus master capture [S-PV3CTX]; the installed Preprod ledger/Plutus API is not established by it (config MinNodeVersion 11.1.0 [P-CONFIG]).\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Exactly the application of this transaction; disappears with the transaction on rollback.\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Mint occurrence only (MCP-CTX-05); issuer identity, backing or redemption is MCP-AST-04@0.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"n/a\",\n      \"status\": \"source-backed-candidate\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"As MCP-CTX-05.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"External observations remain named assumptions [M-CONTRACT].\",\n      \"experiment\": \"n/a\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"Issuer identity, backing, redemption, total supply (MCP-AST-04@0, MCP-AST-03).\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-AST-02@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-AST-02@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F8: v0 asserted a true ledger fact under unsupported-now; split with MCP-AST-04@0\",\n        \"F13\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-META-02\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"META\",\n      \"title\": \"Real-world truth of metadata content\",\n      \"property\": \"Statement type refused: infer the real-world truth of metadata content from its presence in an included transaction.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"anti-pattern\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"n/a\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"B-SCHEMA\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"n/a\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"No ledger mechanism.\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"n/a\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Refuse; at most a named external attestation.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"n/a\",\n      \"status\": \"refused\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"n/a (refused statement type).\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Documents need identity, predicate, trust and freshness assumptions [M-CONTRACT].\",\n      \"experiment\": \"n/a\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"n/a\",\n      \"category\": \"d\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-META-02@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-META-02@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F8: anti-pattern requires refused\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-UNS-02\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"UNS\",\n      \"title\": \"Guard satisfiability / liveness from accepted executions\",\n      \"property\": \"Statement type refused: infer guard satisfiability (usability), liveness or duty discharge from accepted executions.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"anti-pattern\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"n/a\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"T08\",\n        \"M-CONTRACT\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"n/a\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"n/a\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"n/a\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Separate analysis; proofs give safety per accepted transition only.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"n/a\",\n      \"status\": \"refused\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"n/a (refused statement type).\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Safety proofs do not supply liquidity, inclusion or liveness [M-CONTRACT].\",\n      \"experiment\": \"n/a\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"n/a\",\n      \"category\": \"d\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-UNS-02@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-UNS-02@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F8: anti-pattern requires refused\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-XCH-02\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"XCH\",\n      \"title\": \"Bridge message finalized (candidate derived from bridge schema example; not a bridge row)\",\n      \"property\": \"bridge_message_finalized(message_hash, epoch, nullifier) -> bool under a named anchor and finality rule.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"ledger-historical-anchored\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"epoch\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"B-SCHEMA\",\n        \"B-REQ\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"Envelope fields per B-ENVELOPE.\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"Inclusion and finality witnesses.\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"Named anchor_type and finality_rule; consumed-message record.\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Two-part expiry (source age and submission window).\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Typed envelope + registry.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"Named in derived bridge schema only.\",\n      \"status\": \"research-only\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Bridge S01/CONS gates.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Conditional-settlement consumer pattern.\",\n      \"experiment\": \"n/a here.\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"Finality from proof validity (destination must not infer it).\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-XCH-02@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-XCH-02@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F8: title contradicted being a row\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-PROP-01\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"PROP\",\n      \"title\": \"Inductive invariant certificate per action\",\n      \"property\": \"For each action a of P: for all inputs and states, I(pre) and the guards of a imply I(post_a); one quantifier-free bit-vector validity query per action because /1 actions are straight-line. The certificate reports, per action, whether the guard conjunction is satisfiable over the scenario domain; a vacuous certificate (unsatisfiable guards, or a program whose every action refuses through conflicting identities, M-DISPOSITIONS F11 as quoted) is labelled vacuous and never satisfies a policy requiring PROP-01. Domain: all scenarios in the adapter's common subset (M-DISPOSITIONS RP-7 as quoted).\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"universal-property\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"all executions of P under moriarty-core/1\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"T08\",\n        \"M-DISPOSITIONS\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"(program_hash, property_hash, semantics, bounds, checker id) in the certificate.\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"None (public program) or program (private variant).\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"Checker soundness; property formalization is the intended one.\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Valid while program_hash and semantics are unchanged.\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Off-chain, permissionlessly re-checkable certificate; Groth16 only if the program must stay private.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"Core has no property declaration form (per T08).\",\n      \"status\": \"source-backed-candidate\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Property specification form bound by hash.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Contract-property obligation; deploy-time certificate as in historical wiki/formal-assurance (per T08).\",\n      \"experiment\": \"T08 E2: conservation holds; 'every duty decrease paired with payment' fails on bare Discharge with an evaluator-replayed counterexample; unknown/timeout reported as unknown. Vacuity control: a program whose actions all refuse gets vacuous, never pass.\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"Any per-transaction fact; liveness.\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-PROP-01@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-PROP-01@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F8: vacuity label and scenario domain\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-PROP-04\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"PROP\",\n      \"title\": \"Single-thread history compliance by ledger induction\",\n      \"property\": \"For every UTxO carrying thread token tau on fork F observed up to point P: given MCP-LIN-02@1 (policy-script uniqueness), MCP-LIN-09@0 (genesis), PROP-01 for the validator's step relation, and genesis satisfying I, its datum satisfies I. Which UTxOs carry tau on F is itself a ledger observation (provider or anchored); the claim is void under rollback past the observed point.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"derived-history\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"the thread's history on fork F up to observed point P\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"T01\",\n        \"T06\",\n        \"T08\",\n        \"T10\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"Thread policy id, program_hash, property_hash.\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"n/a\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"LIN-01/02; validator correctness; no finality.\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Up to the observed point; void on rollback past it.\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Induction over ledger history; no recursion.\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"None.\",\n      \"status\": \"source-backed-candidate\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"All component rows.\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Scoped history only; all ten tracks agree it does not close MC03/MC06.\",\n      \"experiment\": \"T10 E5(a) two on-chain steps; rollback model (T02 E5) shows claims disappear with the fork.\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"Portable or private history; multi-parent history.\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-PROP-04@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-PROP-04@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F8: derived, fork-relative history claim\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-LED-01\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"LED\",\n      \"title\": \"Past transaction membership under a Mithril CardanoTransactions certificate\",\n      \"property\": \"Transaction hash t is a member of the set committed by cardano_transactions_merkle_root in a certificate whose signed message (with latest_block_number and next AVK) is a valid stake-threshold multisignature chaining to the pinned genesis key.\",\n      \"claimKind\": \"ledger-historical-anchored\",\n      \"temporalScope\": \"up to the certificate's latest_block_number\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"S-MITHCERT\",\n        \"P-MITHCERTS\",\n        \"P-MITHROOT\",\n        \"P-MITHGVK\",\n        \"B-ANCHOR\",\n        \"T02\",\n        \"S-REVIEW-CAT\"\n      ],\n      \"publicInputs\": \"anchor_type mithril_certificate, certificate hash or signed message, t.\",\n      \"privateWitness\": \"Merkle path; certificate chain if verified in circuit.\",\n      \"anchorAndAssumptions\": \"Pinned genesis verification key (commit-pinned; MCP-OBS-04 is main-branch and unpinned). Certificate-chain verification in FullVerification mode, or a named and protected cache declared part of the trust base: under EarlyStop 'anyone able to write to the cache can make the client accept a certificate chain that does not link back to the genesis certificate' [S-MITHCERT source-05.md:110-121 as cited by S-REVIEW-CAT]. Stake-based lottery parameters k=5, m=100, phi_f=0.7 and total_signers 4-10 are aggregator-reported Preprod values (MCP-OBS-03@1); the security level they imply is not derived here and must not be compared with mainnet. The aggregator is untrusted; a network may have a tree of chains from leader and follower aggregators validated by the same genesis key [S-MITHCERT source-05.md:90-95 as cited].\",\n      \"freshnessValidity\": \"Historical; consumer must state acceptable age and Mithril offset (unknown).\",\n      \"strategy\": \"Off-chain client verification, or in-circuit certificate+membership verification wrapped for Cardano (heavy).\",\n      \"implementationEvidence\": \"Entity and certificates observed on Preprod (MCP-OBS-03); nothing verified.\",\n      \"status\": \"conditional-construction\",\n      \"firstBlocker\": \"Pinned verification of one certificate chain (MCP-OBS-03 experiment).\",\n      \"moriartyRelation\": \"Could authenticate a past Cardano event as a Moriarty observation input under a named anchor profile; Moriarty's anchor is local-unqualified today [M-PROFILE].\",\n      \"experiment\": \"Verify a real Preprod tx hash with the aggregator prover and a pinned client; mutate one Merkle sibling and one certificate byte (both must fail).\",\n      \"notEstablished\": \"Slot/height of t, unspentness of its outputs, finality, Moriarty semantics of t.\",\n      \"category\": \"c\",\n      \"versionedId\": \"MCP-LED-01@1\",\n      \"supersedes\": \"MCP-LED-01@0\",\n      \"changeReason\": [\n        \"F9: genesis pin, FullVerification or declared cache trust, aggregator-reported parameters\"\n      ],\n      \"introducedIn\": \"1-draft-20261015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MCP-LED-05\",\n      \"version\": \"1\",\n      \"family\": \"LED\",\n      \"title\": \"Protocol-parameter identity at an epoch\",\n      \"property\": \"Mithril signed messages include a next_protocol_parameters hash; a consumer could bind a parameter-set hash